        <name>applyRelayState</name>
        <qualifiedname>Unit4Relay::applyRelayState</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Applies the staged relay states to the module. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Writes the internal relay state array to the module’s I2C register, turning relays ON or OFF as specified by the states set via <computeroutput>setRelayState()</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">None</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="attention"><para>Requires a prior call to <computeroutput>setRelayState()</computeroutput> to stage the desired relay states. Ensure the module is initialized with <computeroutput><ref refid="class_unit4_relay_1adc660c2e5941b7921e8f32dec1a88172" kindref="member">begin()</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="class_unit4_relay_1aae6e0d7daca1902707378c714047ef65" kindref="member">init()</ref></computeroutput>.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>UNIT_4RELAY_OK</computeroutput>: Success</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>UNIT_4RELAY_ERR_I2C</computeroutput>: I2C communication error </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
